`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h2,{id:"phase-1---understand-how-claude-handles-your-data",children:"Phase 1 - Understand how Claude handles your data"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Nonprofits ask us the same six questions about their data. Each is answered below in plain English, with a link to the public page behind it. This summarizes Anthropic's public documentation and isn't legal advice. If anything here differs from your organization's agreement with Anthropic (for most Team plans, the Commercial Terms you accepted at signup), the agreement governs."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Note your organization's answers as you go, as you will use them in Phase 2."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"team-vs-enterprise",children:"Team vs Enterprise"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Default data handling is the same on both plans: no training on your data by default, same default privacy, same security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, ISO 42001). Both plans have single sign-on (SSO), domain verification and just-in-time (JIT) provisioning (accounts created the first time someone signs in)."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(i,{type:"note",title:"On Enterprise",children:(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Enterprise adds the controls you need once Claude is running across the whole organization. That means identity controls (SCIM to sync staff accounts automatically from your identity provider, such as Okta, Microsoft Entra ID or Google Workspace, and custom roles that decide which groups get which connectors and capabilities) and compliance controls (audit logs, the Compliance API, custom retention, and the ability to process health information under HIPAA)."})}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"1-what-data-goes-into-claude",children:"1. What data goes into Claude?"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:["The data you already have. Claude works with what staff give it: what they type or paste, ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/8241126-upload-files-to-claude",children:"files they upload"})," (spreadsheets, PDFs, documents), and, if you turn ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11176164-use-connectors-to-extend-claude-s-capabilities",children:"connectors"})," on, what it can read from tools like Google Drive or Microsoft 365. It can't reach anything you haven't connected, and with connectors on, it pulls in only what's relevant to what someone asks."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"In practice that looks like a development director uploading last year's gift spreadsheet and asking which lapsed donors to call first, or a program lead pasting in survey responses to find the themes. Start there: the spreadsheets, documents and notes staff already handle every day."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Most of this information is already covered by rules you have today."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"What's new is the conversation history: what staff asked and what Claude answered. The next five questions cover it: whether it's used to train models, who can see it, how long it's kept and where, and what changes when you connect other tools."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(i,{type:"tip",title:"What to put in your policy",children:(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Your confidentiality and data-handling rules for donor records, client files, financials and HR documents still apply when staff use Claude, and your AI policy should reflect that."})}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"2-is-our-data-used-to-train-claude",children:"2. Is our data used to train Claude?"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"No."})," By default, Anthropic does not use conversations (including inputs and outputs), files or connected data from Team or Enterprise accounts to train its models. This is the same on both Team and Enterprise plans. Learn more at our ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://privacy.claude.com/en/articles/7996868-is-my-data-used-for-model-training",children:"Privacy Center"})," and in the ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://www.anthropic.com/legal/commercial-terms",children:"Commercial Terms of Service"}),"."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:["The exception you control: when a staff member clicks thumbs-up or thumbs-down on a response, that conversation is submitted to Anthropic as feedback and may be used to improve Claude (see ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/10504844",children:"Manage user feedback settings"}),"). Owners can turn it on or off, so check how yours is set."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(i,{type:"tip",title:"What to put in your policy",children:(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Decide which, and say so in your policy. Phase 3 comes back to this."})}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"3-who-can-see-our-conversations",children:"3. Who can see our conversations?"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Colleagues."})," Other staff see a conversation only if the person who had it shares it with them. ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/9519189",children:"Sharing a project"})," (a workspace with its own instructions, files and chats) shares its instructions and files, not the chats in it. Each person's chats stay private by default. Owners decide whether projects can be shared or made public (visible to everyone in your organization, not outside it) at all."]}),`
