`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"4-how-long-is-data-kept-and-can-we-delete-it",children:"4. How long is data kept, and can we delete it?"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Conversations stay in your account until the staff member deletes them (or, on Enterprise, your retention period removes them). Once deleted, they leave that person's history immediately and Anthropic's back-end systems within 30 days, except where the law requires longer retention or as described below."}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:["Content that automated systems flag under Anthropic's ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://www.anthropic.com/legal/aup",children:"Usage Policy"})," (Anthropic's own rules for what Claude may be used for, separate from your policy) can be kept for up to two years, and the classification itself (a score, not your content) for up to seven years. This applies to flagged content, not everyday conversations."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:["On ",(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Team"}),", there's no auto-delete: conversations stay until staff delete them."]}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(i,{type:"note",title:"On Enterprise",children:(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Enterprise"})," Owners can set a ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/10440198-configure-custom-data-retention-controls-for-enterprise-plans",children:"custom retention period"})," for the whole organization (minimum 30 days) so conversations auto-delete. Chats inside projects follow a separate project retention period, so set that too."]})}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:["Learn more about ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://privacy.claude.com/en/articles/7996866-how-long-do-you-store-my-organization-s-data",children:"how long Anthropic stores your organization's data"}),"."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"5-where-does-our-data-live-and-who-else-handles-it",children:"5. Where does our data live, and who else handles it?"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:["Data is stored in the United States. By default, processing may route through data centers in the US, Europe, Asia and Australia (Enterprise plans on usage-based billing can restrict inference to the US). See ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://privacy.claude.com/en/articles/7996890-where-are-your-servers-located-do-you-host-your-models-on-eu-servers",children:"where Anthropic's servers are located"}),"."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:["Anthropic uses a published list of ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://trust.anthropic.com/subprocessors",children:"sub-processors"}),": cloud hosting, support, billing and similar vendors. Anthropic posts changes to the Trust Center and gives advance notice of new sub-processors under its ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://www.anthropic.com/legal/data-processing-addendum",children:"Data Processing Addendum"}),"; you can subscribe to the Trust Center news feed."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:["Anthropic holds SOC 2 Type II, ISO 27001:2022 and ISO/IEC 42001:2023 (AI management) certifications. Reports and certificates are available from the Trust Center, some on request. See ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://privacy.claude.com/en/articles/10015870-what-certifications-has-anthropic-obtained",children:"what certifications Anthropic has obtained"}),"."]}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:["Review security details at the ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://trust.anthropic.com/",children:"Anthropic Trust Center"}),"."]}),`
