`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11176164-use-connectors-to-extend-claude-s-capabilities",children:(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Connectors"})})," (Google Drive, Gmail, Microsoft 365, Slack, your CRM via a custom connector, and others) let Claude read from a system when it's relevant to what a staff member asks, and take actions in it if you allow them."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:["In your connected systems, Claude only sees what the user has access to. Take Google Drive: if a staff member can't open a file in Drive, Claude can't open it for them either. Each person signs in to the connected tool with their own account. Two exceptions you'd set up on purpose: a ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11175166-get-started-with-custom-connectors-using-remote-mcp",children:"custom connector"})," (one your IT team or a vendor builds) that uses one shared login reaches whatever that login can access, and with ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/15537633-authorize-mcp-connectors-for-your-entire-organization",children:"enterprise-managed authorization"})," IT authorizes a connector once for everyone. Making a connector available doesn't hand Claude anyone's login."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:["Claude retrieves what's relevant at the time of the request. Whatever it retrieves becomes part of that conversation and follows the same rules as questions 2-5: not used for training by default, visible to other staff only if the conversation is shared and to admins as described in question 3, same retention. The connected service itself still handles your data under its own terms. See ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/10166901",children:"how the Google Workspace connectors handle your data"}),"."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Owners decide which connectors are available at all, what each may do (always allow, needs approval or blocked, per action) and, on Enterprise, which groups get which."})," ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12592343",children:"Desktop extensions"})," in the Claude Desktop app are open by default until you turn on the allowlist. You'll set all of this in Phase 3."]}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12512176-what-are-skills",children:(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Skills"})}),' are packaged instructions and reference files that teach Claude how your organization does a specific task, such as "draft a grant report in our format." ',(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Anything you put in a skill is treated like anything else you give Claude:"})," not used for training by default, visible only where it's shared and to admins as described in question 3. Owners decide who can create, share and publish skills; see ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13119606-provision-and-manage-skills-for-your-organization",children:"provision and manage skills for your organization"}),"."]}),`
