`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:["In every case, by default none of this is used for training, it's visible only to the staff it's shared with and to admins as described in question 3, and your organization is responsible for complying with the laws that apply to its data (see the ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://www.anthropic.com/legal/commercial-terms",children:"Commercial Terms"})," and the ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://www.anthropic.com/legal/data-processing-addendum",children:"Data Processing Addendum"}),")."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Covered by HIPAA?"})," If you're a clinic or a health plan, or you handle health records for one, protected health information (PHI) needs a Business Associate Agreement (BAA) with Anthropic. That's available with the ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13296973-hipaa-ready-enterprise-plans",children:"HIPAA-ready configuration on Enterprise plans"}),", and not on Team. ",(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"On Team"}),", keep PHI out of Claude entirely and use it for everything else: grant writing, board reports, policies, de-identified program summaries. If PHI is central to the work you want help with, ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://claude.com/solutions/nonprofits#pricing",children:"contact our sales team"})," about Enterprise."]}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(i,{type:"note",title:"On Enterprise",children:(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"On Enterprise"}),", you aren't covered automatically. Your Primary Owner turns on HIPAA under Organization settings > Data and privacy > HIPAA Compliance and accepts the BAA in that same flow - there's no separate document to sign. It can't be reversed from organization settings, so read the BAA and the Implementation Guide in the flow before accepting. Once it's on, the BAA covers chat, projects, artifacts and file creation (with limits), but not every feature: connectors and skills can be turned on but aren't covered, and memory is unavailable. Read the Implementation Guide for HIPAA Entities on the Trust Center (summarized in ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://privacy.claude.com/en/articles/8114513-business-associate-agreements-baa-for-commercial-customers",children:"Business Associate Agreements for commercial customers"}),") before you follow the connector and settings steps in Phase 3."]})}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Not sure whether HIPAA applies to you?"})," That depends on the services you provide and who you provide them for. Anthropic can't make that determination for you. Check with your legal counsel or compliance lead before client health details go in."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"When in doubt, ask one question:"})," would I be comfortable if a colleague saw this in a shared project? If not, leave it out or strip the identifying details first. Staff can apply that test without legal training."]}),`
